The counted backlog item (v0.11): the backlog is the framework's ONE counting primitive.
Every self-improvement signal class is captured as a backlog item of the right kind, and the
weekly review-history sweep counts occurrences and routes by kind at threshold:
  - `task`         — a plain one-off (the classic v0 item). Never auto-promoted.
  - `lesson`       — a derivation lesson: something a GENERATOR (a template or design-* skill)
                     should have prevented. At 2 occurrences → an upstream delta targeting the
                     generator (root_cause_target), via propose-to-core.
  - `process-gap`  — recurring work with no covering process. At 2+ runs/occurrences → a
                     design-process draft proposal for the owning dept (v0.12 draft mode).
  - `resource-gap` — a missing tool/access/account blocked or degraded work. At threshold →
                     an acquire-resource candidate (v0.13); until then the count itself is the signal.
Counting fields: `occurrences:` (integer, incremented by whoever re-observes the signal — capture
conventions live in chief-of-staff.md) and `last_seen:` (ISO date). Both OPTIONAL and additive —
v0 items without them remain valid (absent = occurrences: 1).
