# <<ITEM_TITLE>>

## Goal

What outcome this backlog item is trying to produce (for `lesson`/`process-gap`/`resource-gap`: what the signal was, and what would prevent or cover it). One short paragraph.

## Acceptance

How we know a single run succeeded — concrete, observable criteria. For signal kinds: what "resolved" looks like (generator constraint shipped / process adopted / resource granted).

## Runs log

An audit trail of executions and re-observations. When the owner decides a `task` item is ready to formalize, they invoke `design-process`; `lesson`/`process-gap`/`resource-gap` items are swept and routed automatically by the weekly `review-history` run at their thresholds.

